<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Golden Bull of 1222</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1222">1222</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull</a> of 1222 was a charter issued by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-ii-of-hungary">Andrew II of Hungary</a> under pressure from the lesser nobility and royal servants, who were angered by his lavish grants of royal estates. It guaranteed their freedom from taxation and arbitrary arrest, limited military service abroad and gave nobles a right to resist a king who broke its terms. It is often compared with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a> as an early limit on royal power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1222.jpg" alt="Golden Bull of 1222" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:II._Andr%C3%A1s_aranybull%C3%A1ja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
